{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC2 — three RED demonstrations. Each violation was injected, measured, and reverted; the\nworking tree is clean of all of them.\n\nEvery one reproduces the SAME signature the bug describes: the documented local pre-flight\nreturns 0, and the gate CI runs returns 1.\n\n1) Stale entry in .github/mechanism-baseline.json (injected for the demo only — never a fix):\n     make lint EXIT=0\n     pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py EXIT=1\n     FAILED test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree\n       assert set(baseline) | admitted == live\n   This is the extra bite over `--check`, which make lint DOES run: --check tolerates a\n   stale entry (it buckets as 'stale', which is the ratchet's allowed direction); only the\n   test asserts the union equality.\n\n2) Dropped the `[ -f ]` guard from the 'comment-hygiene gate' step of _build-and-test.yml:\n     make lint EXIT=0\n     pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py EXIT=1\n     FAILED test_completeness_every_gate_step_is_guarded_or_marked\n       .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml :: [lint] 'comment-hygiene gate' runs\n       scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py with no `-f` guard and no marker\n\n3) Added a defined, exported public symbol (`demo_surface_drift`) to rebar.__all__:\n     make lint EXIT=0\n     make typecheck EXIT=0\n     pytest tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py EXIT=1\n     FAILED test_committed_baseline_matches_live_surface\n       Public API surface drift detected against the committed baseline\n   Note: a first attempt used an UNDEFINED name and make lint exited 2 (ruff F822), which\n   would have been a fake demonstration — the point is a tree that lint calls clean. Redone\n   with a real definition placed in isort order so RUF022 also passes; only then is lint 0.\n\nAC3 — the git-add skew, closed at the source. Wrote a new unguarded gate step referencing a\nNEW, untracked scripts/check_demo_skew.py, then ran the completeness check in three states:\n     OLD tracked-only listing, script UNSTAGED  -> PASSED   <- the false green\n     NEW listing,               script UNSTAGED -> FAILED\n     NEW listing,               script STAGED   -> FAILED\nSo the verdict is now a property of the tree rather than of the index. The change is strictly\nwidening (--cached --others --exclude-standard), so it can only turn a false green red; a\n.gitignore'd path is still excluded, pinned by the new regression test."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788515665446784001,"uuid":"5b3b8414-ebb3-4a16-805b-4f013d37499b"}